  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2ee87e681215b6147a44021cf30db039, type: 3}
  m_Name: 3.University of Malta Valletta Campus
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  nameOfPoint: University of Malta Valletta Campus
  coordinatesPoint: {x: 14.515757, y: 35.8986}
  firstPartInfo: "Going through the <link=Image_5><u><color=blue>records</link></u></color>,
    I find Ondina\u2019s name in a class register from the 1930s."
  secondPartInfo: "Seeing this, I dig deeper to find more about her. In 1933, Ondina
    Tayar graduated with a Pharmaceutical Chemist [Ph.C.] diploma from the University
    of Malta. At that time, the University of Malta\u2019s main campus was in Valletta,
    before it was moved to Msida in 1964. Her graduation was significant because
    she was one of the first women to obtain this specific degree from the University
    of Malta.\r\n\r\nLooking through the university\u2019s library, I find a book
    written by a descendant of the Tayar family, Aline P\u2019Nina Tayar. I ask to
    borrow it and sift through the pages to find Ondina\u2019s name. It is written
    that although her graduation was a great achievement in the eyes of her father
    Banino, her mother Rachele was opposed to it, fearing that her daughter\u2019s
    independence would lead to an incident like that in the Archbishop\u2019s Palace."
  imgMarker: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c98feaebd40d8df449e6d3855ac84352, type: 3}
  imgMain: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c983d07e6602bf144a5cc058a20228eb, type: 3}
  nameOfStory: Jewish
  hintOfPOI: "The book\u2019s story seems to be leading me to the Archbishop\u2019s
    Palace."
  solutionOfPOI: "The Archbishop\u2019s Palace does keep  its own records. They could
    have something more about this."
